$vb(P_1) dot vb(P_2)$ is invariant under Lorentz transformations, so work in the rest frame of $vb(P_2)$, where $vb(P_1) = vec(E_1 \/ c, vb(p)_1)$ and $vb(P_2) = vec(m_2 c, vb(0))$. Hence $vb(P_1) dot vb(P_2) = m_2 E_1$, and since $E_1 = sqrt(p_1^2 c^2 + m_1^2 c^4) >= m_1 c^2$, the bound follows.

The positive sign of the square root is chosen: the other sign would give a negative kinetic energy in the non-relativistic limit, and proper orthochronous Lorentz transformations preserve positivity of $E_1$.
